<h2>Bottom line</h2>
<p>A MUD tax pays for the water, sewer and drainage that made a newer Texas subdivision possible. Before you buy, look up the district on the appraisal district site, read the seller's notice to purchasers line by line, compare bonds approved with bonds issued, and judge the home on its total tax rate rather than the MUD line alone. For more on local rates, see our guide to the <a href="/blog/houston-property-tax-rate/">Houston property tax rate</a> and browse <a href="/category/homeownership/">homeownership guides</a>.</p>
